# Local benchmark credentials — template. Copy to `.env` and fill in the providers you have.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored (never commit it); only this `.env.example` is tracked, and it must stay
# secret-free (the repo-checks secret-hygiene gate scans tracked files). Bun auto-loads `.env` when
# you run a bin (e.g. `bun apps/cli/src/bin/bench-smoke.ts e2b memory`), so these become process.env.
#
# You do NOT need every provider: a missing credential is recorded as a skip, not a failure. CI reads
# these from the GitHub Environment `privileged`, never from a committed file — see docs/ci-secrets.md.

# --- e2b (https://e2b.dev) ---
E2B_API_KEY=

# --- Daytona (https://daytona.io) ---
DAYTONA_API_KEY=
# Runner target / region the sandbox boots in. Defaults to us-west-2 when unset (the active region);
# the account default has no `container` runners, so leave this as us-west-2 unless you know otherwise.
DAYTONA_TARGET=us-west-2

# --- Modal (https://modal.com) ---
MODAL_TOKEN_ID=
MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET=

# --- Blaxel (https://blaxel.ai) ---
BL_API_KEY=
BL_WORKSPACE=

# --- Novita (https://novita.ai) — E2B-protocol-compatible control plane ---
NOVITA_API_KEY=

# --- Namespace (https://namespace.so) ---
# A token FILE, not a bare token: @computesdk/namespace reads {"bearer_token": "..."} JSON from the path
# in NSC_TOKEN_FILE. The harness gate is a strict AND over the vars below, so a bare NSC_TOKEN alone
# still skips even though the SDK's own fallback chain would accept it — mint a file instead. After
# `nsc auth login` (https://namespace.so/docs), mint the same least-privilege, revocable token CI uses:
#
#   nsc token create --token_file "$HOME/.nsc-bench-token.json" \
#     --grant '{"resource_type":"instance","resource_id":"*","actions":["create","list","get","destroy","exec"]}'
#
# then point this at that path. CI needs no stored secret at all: it federates through GitHub's OIDC
# identity (nscloud-setup + `nsc auth exchange-github-token`) and mints the token per job.
# Keep the token file OUTSIDE this repo — the secret-hygiene gate fails CI on tracked credential files.
NSC_TOKEN_FILE=

# --- Microsandbox (https://microsandbox.dev) ---
# Explicit opt-in for host-local libkrun runs. The host needs KVM on Linux or
# Hypervisor.framework on macOS; keep unset on ordinary CI runners.
MICROSANDBOX_LOCAL_BENCH=
# Cloud runs require only MSB_API_KEY, which stays in the control-plane client and never enters the
# benchmark guest. Set MSB_API_URL only to override the SDK default for staging or private deployments.
MSB_API_KEY=
MSB_API_URL=

# --- Optional overrides (leave unset for the pinned public toolchain) ---
# Point the adapters at a specific toolchain image / template instead of the canonical published one.
# Useful only when iterating on the toolchain locally; see packages/providers/src/lib/config.ts.
# BENCH_TOOLCHAIN_IMAGE=
# E2B_TEMPLATE=
# DAYTONA_SNAPSHOT=
# NOVITA_TEMPLATE=
# The daytona-container variant needs its OWN snapshot (a Daytona snapshot's sandbox class is fixed at
# bake time) and reads its own region var; both default to the version-scoped name / us-west-2.
# DAYTONA_CONTAINER_TARGET=us-west-2
# DAYTONA_CONTAINER_SNAPSHOT=
